STANDING ORDERS (Suggi, 2026-11-15 and 2026-11-16; set and changed by him alone)
S1. Explore freely.
S2. Grow income; optimize the routes and the credits per hour.
S3. Evolve the fleet.
S4. Build bases and stations.
S5. Grow the fleet and the faction.
S6. A base, and a station in a system of ours when we are ready: gather the materials and the supply for it and get the economy going (Suggi, 2026-11-16: "i want a base build and the materials gathered and all ready to build a station in a system when ready").
Every member works toward these on every turn, also where no order below names the work. The orders below (GOAL, FLEET, TURN and the blocks) are the Fleet Admiral's reading of them: the steps, the subgoals, who does what and the limits. The limits are Suggi's own words too and stand beside the standing orders: the stance (F2), no word to another player (F4), no new pilot without his word (F5), the wallet floor (F7), the money limit (F12), the faction's affairs (F11). An order below that seems to stand in the way of a standing order is a request to the Fleet Admiral, never a reason to pass a limit.
GOAL (the steps toward the standing orders; Suggi, 2026-11-15)
Phase 1 of the strategy (governance/strategy.md, section V): income. First income that repeats in every division. Then a faction with shared storage and a first supply chain. Then stations and bases of our own beyond the safe zone: strong and independent, not hiding. Every order below serves the first step. What the third step costs (the game's guides, read 2026-11-15): an outpost in a lawless system is an Outpost Kit and 100,000 cr, a full station a Station Core and 5,000,000 cr, in a system without empire and police, at a place without a station; a faction may hold eight outposts and five stations. More ships are born when a division shows paying work for more ships than it has (F5). Where we stand (`hive.py fleet`, 2026-11-16 01:43 UTC): the first hour of steady money above zero, +55,031 cr, made by 10 miners on ice and 5 hunters, while 120 of 146 ships wait docked. The bottleneck of this turn is a tool, not a field and not a bid (`hive.py capacity`, 01:30 UTC): five of our stations bid for 81,695 units of water ice, 254,347 units lie in the fields we read, and 14 ships carry an Ice Harvester I. The earners are the 40 miners, 20 traders and 20 haulers; harvesters go to the miners first. Three ways to the tool, all taken at once: (a) bought at our stations, 14 on offer at 1,413 to 1,738 cr, a few at each (books of 01:20 to 01:26 UTC); (b) bought at Ironlight Crossroads in LHS 1140, the one foreign market, 20 on offer at 638 cr (one book, 01:24 UTC); (c) made by hand from 4 steel plate, 2 circuit board, 3 flex polymer and 1 power cell (`craftbook.py item ice_harvester_i`): steel plate and circuit boards from the ore we hold; flex polymer stands on offer from 129 cr or is made from caustic sac or from silicon and nickel ore; a power cell is made from 2 circuit boards, 3 energy crystals and 2 copper wiring, or from creature goods. Made from stored ore by Logistics for Mining, it is the first supply chain of the fleet. A bid is used up as we sell into it and its refill is not measured: the bids are the next limit to watch. An Outpost Kit stood on offer for 216,825 cr at Ironlight Crossroads (one order book): with the fee an outpost would cost about 317,000 cr without the facility that makes the kit (`hive.py base outpost`). Founding one is Suggi's decision; no ship buys the kit. Suggi, 2026-11-16: the kit is not needed now; a base is built later. Where we stand at 02:49 UTC, after the engine's restart of 02:00 UTC ended the runs in flight: 18 ships at work, 120 waiting. In the last four hours mining made 4,696 cr per ship-hour flown, hunting 1,771, and the fleet 175 cr per ship-hour over all 146 ships; the scale is the best route at 8,271 (the tool fleet with view=tasks). What a bid regains is now measured at its best price (view=refill): water ice at Central Nexus at least 1,628 units an hour, at Node Alpha at least 870; the deepest standing bid seen is 67,735 units at Central Nexus at 21 to 23 cr. Tools on offer in our books at 02:44 UTC: 34 Ice Harvesters, 82 Gas Harvesters. At 04:52 UTC: 66 ships at work, 80 docked; steady net 104,094 cr in the last hour (49,065 an hour over six); 47 Ice Harvesters and 3 Gas Harvesters fitted (14 and 0 at 01:40 UTC); mining made 3,809 cr per ship-hour flown, hunting 1,332, the fleet 315 over all 146 ships. At 06:50 UTC (the tool fleet, views money and tasks): 60 ships at work, 86 docked; steady net 149,095 cr in the last hour and 79,803 an hour over six; the fleet 541 credits per ship-hour over all 146 ships in four hours, against the best repeating route, mine-ruchbah-ice-belt, at 9,785; the route maker's list stood three hours old until 06:36 UTC (errors.log ENT-044), so the turns of 04:00 UTC named no new test. (d) The station (S6). What it takes is printed by the tool base_plan with kind=station, from the catalog and our stock: a fee of 5,000,000 cr and one station core; the core is made only in a station core foundry of level 4, which costs 38,000,000 cr and, among others, 12,500 steel plate, 8,400 hull plating and 7,800 copper piping to build; 43,000,000 cr in all, 28 of its 30 raw inputs short today (iron ore: 491,400 needed, 59,658 held), and no finished core on offer in our books. That is 400 to 900 hours of income at the rates of this hour and of the last six: the way to the station is income first (strategy, phase 1) and the faction's storage (F11), and each division reads its part of the list now (one line in each block), so that the fleet knows where every input comes from before it has the credits. An outpost (100,000 cr and a kit) is the small first base; Suggi decides when.
FLEET
F1. Each Admiral commands the ships of its own division, by the word before the dash of a pilot's name: miner- Zero, trader- Mercury, hauler- Apollo, drone- Apophis, scout- Oracle. The Fleet Admiral commands the command group (F10) and may command any ship. Every command goes through the scripts of game/fleet/ (game/fleet/index.md): they refuse a ship of another division and a ship another program is flying. No call goes to the gate around them.
