sus to a ship); the history store drawn in queue.log ENT-058 (one writer, a read copy for the tools); a record of every bid's whole ladder and of the asks, so that a refill is measured in full; a short form of the standing fleet; the nine changes owed above. I report to Suggi after each of my turns. Since ENT-011, done: the runner fault of the chain (my own, of 01:09 UTC) and a row for every crashed run; the sale step of mine.py; `requires.booked`; holds in the tool stock; the tools' server answers through the file on disk, and its search works; the station's Metrics page holds still; `scripts/fleet-build.sh` and the skill fleet-build. Done in my turn of 06:30 UTC: the route maker runs again (it failed every pass from 03:32 to 06:32 UTC) and one bad file costs only its own reading; a service that is down or fails its passes is named in my chat within five minutes by itself; `requires.skills` (ENT-109); the fill gate counts only work a role may take (ENT-095); the battle stance flee on `in_battle` and the hold-back of a pilot stuck at stop 1 (ENT-090); the hunt step's last word in the run row (ENT-092); the scale of the tool fleet's view tasks is a repeating route. Owed in my turn of 10:30 UTC, inside 12:00 UTC: an engine loop without an order file ended by the dispatcher (ENT-083); a herd floor for a circuit's hunt step (Apophis, his report of 05:27 UTC); craft inputs booked as money spent once (Apollo, his report of 05:29 UTC); the battle stance flee in census.py and mine.py. For S6 and F11: the lockbox's and the offices' live costs, the purse script (F20), and base_plan kept current.
