you write as a script before the next, and a fix of a runner's step you build yourself. From ENT-014, four more. (a) Every route of yours that sells one good into one station's bid names that bid: `requires.bid` {item, base, min_price} (game/routes/BLUEPRINT.md); the dispatcher closes it while a book read within the hour shows the bid gone and opens it when one shows it back, so a route set `status: off` for a bid that left comes back on with the field instead. (b) The dispatcher closes by itself a repeating route whose last three runs inside six hours each lost money, whatever its six-hour sum, and the fill gate no longer counts it as paying work; a route your hand took out for that reason may stand in the plan again. (c) The once line of the Central Nexus board stands in every plan, in this order, each gated by its route: voidborn-first-steps-board (accepts First Steps), voidborn-network-expansion, voidborn-collective-provides, voidborn-signal-protocol (fill with action=add and first=true; their files and limits are Mercury's). voidborn-first-steps is off: it served only pilots that already held the mission; drop it from your plan. (d) A circuit's hunt step may name `min_creatures`: no pilot is sent while the place's census counts fewer. A once route whose every stop was skipped no longer counts as done for its pilot; an engine loop no runner owns is stopped by the dispatcher after five minutes.
